 "source_type": "instagram",
 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DfZziL7I42m/",
 "title": "Ask for the things you want",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "The creator explains that you must be willing to ask for what you want in life in a kind and mindful way. She shares a personal restaurant story to demonstrate how polite and direct requests can lead to positive results.",
 "key_points": [
  "You have to be willing to ask for the things you want in this life.",
  "You can ask without being overly aggressive while still being kind and mindful of the other person.",
  "The kinder you are, the more inclined someone will be to say yes or make something work for you.",
  "Example phrasing to use with a server: \"Could you look into this further? Something seems incorrect here. I would appreciate if you could look into it more.\"",
  "Bottom line: closed mouths don't get fed, and you should feel empowered and capable of asking for what you want."
 ],
 "content": "Ask!! 🗣️ You can have the audacity while staying kind, considerate, and charming! Don’t ever let anyone tell you you can’t be both. 💅🏻 Jewelry is @atoleajewelry ✨ #wellwithraele #socialskills #confidence #communicationskills\n\nYou have to be willing to ask for the things you want in this life in order to get the things you want in this life. And there is a way to do this without being a bitch, without being overly aggressive, while still being kind and being mindful of the other person. And actually, the kinder you are, the more inclined someone will be to say \"yes\" or to try to make something work for you. I was out at a restaurant recently. It was my husband's birthday, so I was treating, and something seemed off on the bill, so I asked our server, \"Could you look into this further? Something seems incorrect here. I would appreciate if you could look into it more.\" And she did. And not only did she correct the thing I initially called out, but she gave us free dessert because it was my husband's birthday. So it's actually a double win that wouldn't have happened at all if I didn't call out the initial thing to begin with. I honestly wasn't even thinking about the dessert or thinking of getting it for free because it was a birthday. She brought it up on her own and seemed happy to include it in her revision. And of course, I made sure to tip on the original bill amount. You should feel empowered to ask for the things that you want and articulate it in a confident, kind way. Let me know if you want more examples for how to tee up your requests in a way that sounds natural to you, you can practice them a few times just to get used to hearing yourself say them. Bottom line closed mouths don't get fed, and you should feel empowered and capable of asking for the things that you want in this life. Bye.\n\nText shown on screen: ASK FOR THE THINGS YOU WANT",
